heta{}_{rr}$ and $\\Gamma^\\phi{}_{tr}$, which is why the diagram is drawn on the axis. There $g^{rr} = \\Delta/\\Sigma$ vanishes at both roots of $\\Delta$, $r_\\pm = GM/c^2 \\pm \\sqrt{(GM/c^2)^2 - a^2}$, and the cones close at both; between them they point to smaller $r$, following the ingoing family.","The domain of the chart begins at $r_+$, the outer zero of $g^{rr}$, and below it the drawing is hatched. On the axis the ergosurface touches the horizon, so the plane stays Lorentzian, and the Kretschmann scalar stays finite at $r = 0$, because the ring singularity lies in the equatorial plane."],"source":{"fields":["coords","parameters","metric_components","inverse_metric_components","kretschmann","domains"],"version":"b081ab1688563fa7"}}]}}
